Hi,

I was wondering if anyone did any work on DKMS for Rust kernel
drivers. I'd love to see all of our new Linux drivers use Rust going
forward, but the one thing I don't have a good handle on is how to
make those drivers available for older kernels. With C we write the
driver, submit it to main and write some thin shim for older kernels
on LTS distros (Ubuntu LTS releases, RHEL, SLES...) which we provide
alongside the driver as DKMS. With Rust the DKMS packages would have
to install rust, ship, basically, with all of the linux/rust/* plus
the shim for "linux/rust" to build/work on all those older kernels. It
seems like having the Linux Rust code be compatible with a few of
those LTS kernels and having an easy way to add DKMS would be highly
beneficial to a lot of people writing new drivers in Rust.

Has anyone done any work on or thought about supporting multiple
kernel versions in Linux Rust drivers?

z

